<problem>
<!-- <title>Derivative of alpha function and similar</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="n" from="2" to=" 7" />
<selectFromSequence name="b_sub" from="-5" to=" 5" exclude="0" />
<selectFromSequence name="reciprocal" from="-1" to=" 1" step=" 2" />
<select name="f">f g h </select>
<select name="x">y z t </select>

<math name="b" simplify="full">$b_sub ^$reciprocal </math>
<math name="bx" simplify="true">$b$x</math>
<math name="fun">$x ^$n *e^(<math simplify="true">$b *$x</math> )</math>
<math name="dfun" simplify="numbers"><math simplify="true">($n *$x ^($n -1) + $b *$x ^$n )</math>*e^($bx )</math>
<math name="monomial" simplify="full">$x ^$n </math>
<math name="exponential" simplify="full">e^($b *$x )</math>
<math name="d_monomial" simplify="full">$n *$x ^($n -1)</math>
<math name="d_exponential" simplify="numbers">$b *e^($bx )</math>

<select name="deriv">
  <option>
    <math>d$f / d$x</math>
  </option>
  <option>
    <math referencesAreFunctionSymbols="$f">$f'($x)</math>
  </option>
</select>

<select name="wording">1 2 3 4 5</select>
</setup>

<conditionalContent>
  <case condition="$wording=1">
    <p>Compute the derivative, <m>$deriv[1][1] </m>, of
    <me>$f($x) = $fun.</me>
    <m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$dfun</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=2">
  <p>Calculate the derivative of
    <me>$f($x) = $fun.</me></p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$dfun</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=3">
  <p>For the function
    <me>$f($x) = $fun,</me>
    what is the derivative $deriv[1][1]?</p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$dfun</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=4">
  <p>Let <m>$f($x) = $fun.</m>  What is the derivative of <m>$f($x)</m>?</p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$dfun</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
  <case condition="$wording=5">
    <p>Compute the derivative, <m>$deriv[1][1] </m>, of the function <m>$f($x)</m> below
    <me>$f($x) = $fun.</me></p>
    <p><m>$deriv[1][1]  =</m> 
    <answer forceFullCheckworkButton="true">$dfun</answer>
    </p>
  </case>
</conditionalContent>





<solution>


Since <m>$f ($x )</m> is the product of <m>$monomial </m> times <m>$exponential </m>, we must use the product rule.  The derivative of <m>$monomial </m> is
<me>\left($monomial \right)' = $d_monomial ,</me>
and the derivative of <m>$exponential </m> is
<me>\left($exponential \right)' = $d_exponential</me>

The derivative of <m>$f ($x )</m> is therefore
<me>$deriv[1][1]  = <math>$d_monomial $exponential  + $monomial $d_exponential</math> = $dfun</me>
</solution>


</problem>